#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "Building Simple Databases"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To learn the basics of &kexi;, you could build a simple database utilizing "
"most elementary &kexi;'s features. To make things simpler, advanced database "
"design topics will not be covered here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start by creating a new empty <emphasis>Phone Book</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Having a new empty database project, perform the following steps:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Design database tables. Read <xref linkend=\"designing-tables\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter data into tables. Read <xref linkend=\"entering-data-into-tables\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "Design database queries. Read <xref linkend=\"designing-queries\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "Design forms. Read <xref linkend=\"designing-forms\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use forms to enter data. Read <xref linkend=\"entering-data-using-forms\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid "Designing Database Tables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, there will be two tables added to your database: <emphasis>persons</"
"emphasis> and <emphasis>phone_numbers</emphasis>. These are exactly the same "
"tables as described in chapter <link linkend=\"database-and-spreadsheet"
"\">Database and spreadsheet</link>. A layout for <emphasis>Persons</"
"emphasis> can be found in section <link linkend=\"data-integrity-and-validity"
"\">Data integrity and validity</link> in that chapter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Table...</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the Menubar. You can also use the button "
"<guilabel>Create object: table</guilabel> on the <link linkend=\"project-"
"navigator-pane\">Project Navigator's toolbar</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Table Designer's window will appear. Looking at the top of designer's "
"window you will notice that &kexi; proposed you a generic name like "
"<emphasis>template</emphasis> for the new table. The table design is not "
"saved yet so you will be able to assign more proper name later. Moreover, "
"because of the same reason, the table name is not yet visible in the <link "
"linkend=\"project-navigator-pane\">Project Navigator</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Table Designer window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Table Designer window consists of following columns:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>PK</guilabel> - Primary Key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Field Caption</guilabel> - caption of the field which will be "
"displayed during data entering."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Data Type</guilabel> - a combo box containing a list of data "
"types, allowing to set a main rule for entered data for a given field. For "
"example, when an integer number data type is set for a field, a database "
"user will not able to enter letter characters into this field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Comments</guilabel> - you can enter here any information useful "
"for understanding what the given field is provided for. This additional text "
"will be saved within the table design and only visible in design mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Table designer</guilabel> window, every row corresponds to "
"a single table field. You can recognize you are in <emphasis>design mode</"
"emphasis> because the <guibutton>Switch to design view</guibutton> button is "
"toggled on within the main &kexi; toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Designing the <emphasis>Persons</emphasis> table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the first row click on the cell in the <guilabel>Field Caption</guilabel> "
"column and enter <emphasis>Name</emphasis> as field caption."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notes about field names and captions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every table field must have a name and a caption, these cannot be empty."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Field name is a word used by the database, usually not visible for users of "
"the database application. The name may not contain special (national) "
"characters (like ±, ¶, Ü) or space characters. The name must only contain "
"roman letters, numbers and underscore sign &quot;_&quot;. Use the latter "
"instead of spaces or dashes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Field names must be started with a letter or underscore sign &quot;_&quot;, "
"never with a number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It does not matter whether you are using small or capital letters. For "
"&kexi; the database name &quot;Persons&quot; is the same as &quot;"
"persons&quot;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Field caption, on the other hand, allows you to enter any letters and "
"special characters. It will be displayed for users of the database "
"application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: building.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "In a similar way, enter the following fields into the table design:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: building.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "surname"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "street"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "house_number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "city"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the above fields, except <emphasis>house_number</emphasis>, are of type "
"<emphasis>text</emphasis>. Change <emphasis>house_number</emphasis> field's "
"type to <emphasis>integer number</emphasis>. To do this, click on a cell in "
"the <guilabel>Data Type</guilabel> column, <emphasis>house_number</emphasis> "
"row and then click on drop down list's button (you can also press "
"<keycombo><keycap>F4</keycap></keycombo> or <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<keycap>Down</keycap></keycombo>. The list of data types will appear. Select "
"the <emphasis>Integer number</emphasis> type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From now on, the <emphasis>house_number</emphasis> field only accepts "
"numbers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Persons</emphasis> table design is ready. Click <guibutton>Switch "
"to data view</guibutton> button on the toolbar to finish designing and "
"switch to Data View for the table. This allows you entering data into the "
"table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As the design is not yet saved in the database, the <guibutton>Save Object "
"As</guibutton> dialog window appears. You need to specify the name for the "
"new table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kexi; offers a generic name like <emphasis>Table1</emphasis>. To change the "
"name, enter <emphasis>Persons</emphasis> into the <emphasis>Caption</"
"emphasis> field and press the <keycombo> <keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo> "
"key or click the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button. The <guilabel>Caption</"
"guilabel> field will be used to display the table to database end-users, "
"&eg; as a form. Unlike the name, the caption can contain any characters "
"including spaces and special characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that filling the <guilabel>Caption</guilabel> field automatically fills "
"the <guilabel>Name</guilabel> field. For your convenience the rule for using "
"only letters, numbers and the &quot;_&quot; character is kept. You can alter "
"the contents of the <guilabel>Name</guilabel> field if you want to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are asked about an agreement for automatic adding of primary key to the "
"table. Click <guibutton>Add primary key</guibutton> button to continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Persons</emphasis> table has been created and opened in Data "
"View. Its name appears in the <guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel> pane."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create the <emphasis>phone_numbers</emphasis> table, in a similar way as "
"<emphasis>persons</emphasis> table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a <emphasis>person</emphasis> field of type <emphasis>Integer number</"
"emphasis> and <emphasis>phone</emphasis> of type <emphasis>Text</emphasis>. "
"Do not use a number type here because phone numbers can have many different "
"forms and prefixes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: building.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Switch to data view</guibutton> button on the toolbar and "
"enter <emphasis>Phones</emphasis> caption for the table. As for your "
"previous table, allow &kexi; to automatically create a primary key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: chapter
#: building.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&enteringdataintotables; &querydesigning; &designingforms; "
"&enteringdatausingforms;"
msgstr ""
